NIGHT_QUESTIONS BE, the tester's 49805 note (b): in the list Excel, a row
whose need column names one of the owner's contacts as a helper also said
„შენს კონტაქტებში არავინ" and „გზა არ არის". Those are about reaching the
listed person, and an owner reads them as a contradiction.

With SEE_HELPER_ON, those two cells say „იხ. დამხმარე" (en/ru/es drafted
alike) on such a row. A row with a real way in, or a state other than
no_route, is unchanged.

OFF in this commit. The words are new text in the owner's file and wait for
Misho's yes.

DONE WHEN (once on): the 4160 file's helper rows read „იხ. დამხმარე" in
the way-in and state columns; every other row is as before.

